('9e63d050-6ac4-5335-b042-c9013860f7fe'::uuid,'est2','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"[Table: CP-c25-32 — daily travel times over a 40-day period. Bus A: 44 min → 5, 45 → 10, 47 → 15, 48 → 10. Bus B: 25 min → 5, 30 → 10, 35 → 15, 40 → 10]\nThe tables give the distribution of daily travel times between two towns for bus A and bus B over a 40-day period. Which statement correctly compares the standard deviations of travel times for bus A and bus B?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"The standard deviation of travel times for bus A is less than the standard deviation of travel times for bus B."},{"key":"B","text":"The standard deviation of travel times for bus B is less than the standard deviation of travel times for bus A."},{"key":"C","text":"The standard deviation of travel times for bus A is equal to the standard deviation of travel times for bus B."},{"key":"D","text":"There is not enough information to compare these standard deviations."}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"panda.md","source_sha256":"e120378a8127836a41962876a763889bbb1df92d70c90242206130acfa43e008","source_question_id":"CP-c25-32","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/CP-c25-32.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for CP-c25-32","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"A"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from panda.md (CP-c25-32)."'::jsonb),
('1ee59da1-3cf3-5856-a4d4-2a0741a30738'::uuid,'est2','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'easy','grid_in','"[Figure: CP-c25-33 — two histograms, Data set X and Data set Y, each of 25 whole numbers from 70 to 100 in intervals of 5. Set X: 70–75 → 9, 75–80 → 6, 80–85 → 6, 85–90 → 4. Set Y: 80–85 → 4, 85–90 → 6, 90–95 → 6, 95–100 → 9]\nThe histograms shown summarize two data sets, X and Y. Each data set consists of 25 whole numbers. In each histogram, the first interval represents the frequency of whole numbers greater than or equal to 70, but less than 75. The second interval represents the frequency of whole numbers greater than or equal to 75, but less than 80, and so on. What is the largest possible difference between the median of data set Y and the mean of data set X?"'::jsonb,'[]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"panda.md","source_sha256":"e120378a8127836a41962876a763889bbb1df92d70c90242206130acfa43e008","source_question_id":"CP-c25-33","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/CP-c25-33.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for CP-c25-33","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"18"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from panda.md (CP-c25-33)."'::jsonb),
('33d2a537-4119-55aa-b2d1-43093493525b'::uuid,'est2','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'easy','mcq','"A digital marketing agency has three groups of clients. The first group consists of 8 clients who are charged a monthly fee of at least $170 but no more than $190. The second group consists of 11 clients who are charged a monthly fee of at least $200 but no more than $230. The third group consists of 21 clients who are charged a monthly fee of at least $240 but no more than $300. If a new client who is charged a monthly fee of $250 is added to the third group, what will be the effect on the mean monthly fee charged by the agency?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"The mean will increase."},{"key":"B","text":"The mean will decrease."},{"key":"C","text":"The mean will remain the same."},{"key":"D","text":"There is not enough information to determine how the mean will change. ## CHAPTER 26 — Statistics II ### Exercise 1"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"panda.md","source_sha256":"e120378a8127836a41962876a763889bbb1df92d70c90242206130acfa43e008","source_question_id":"CP-c25-34","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from panda.md (CP-c25-34)."'::jsonb),
